st views in order to spark what he  called a violent revolution for the  white race Matthews lawyer called his  statements free speech mr. Matthews  statements should be considered in the  context of in exercising his First  Amendment rights the arrests broke up  one plot but Ryan Thorp says the base as  a disparate group of cells remains  dangerous there's indication they had  every intention of carrying out violence  on people and I don't think we should be  cavalier about the level of violence  that could have perpetrated had law  enforcement not acted and remember the  trio down in Georgia with an FBI agent  on the inside they were arrested - and  there was one more twist the FBI says  one of them got worried about Matthews  believing he was a threat to their  broader operation and spoke of killing  him in the end the FBI not only may have  prevented violence at the gun rally they  may have saved Patrick Matthews life  Erik Sorensen Global News Toronto still  ahead the rocky airplane landing that  will have you on the edge of yours  seat  a powerful storm is battering Britain  with hurricane-force winds and so much  rain that more than 200 flood warnings  are in place across the UK  rushing water ripped through the streets  of this town in Yorkshire and it's a  similar scene in many other places train  travel has been brought to a halt by  floodwaters and high winds and just  imagine being a passenger on this plane  as it tried to land in those punishing  winds the storm forced a flight from  Warsaw to London to divert to Birmingham  where it touched down swerving side to  side and then landed with a bounce the  storm has caused hundreds of flight  delays and cancellations in the UK and  across Europe there is political turmoil  in Ireland an exit poll suggests a dead  heat after yesterday's parliamentary  elections ballot counting is still under  way but the poll indicates the Prime  Minister centrist finna Gale party is  neck-and-neck with the opposition Fionn